      "text": "To determine when Wanda, Darren, Beatrice, and Chi will next be together tutoring in the lab, we need to find the least common multiple (LCM) of their work intervals. Darren works every third school day, so the LCM we need is the LCM of 3, 4, 6, and 7.\n\nThe prime factorizations of these numbers are:\n- \\(3 = 3\\)\n- \\(4 = 2^2\\)\n- \\(6 = 2 \\times 3\\)\n- \\(7 = 7\\)\n\nThe LCM is found by taking the highest power of each prime number that appears in the factorizations:\n- The highest power of 2 is \\(2^2\\) (from 4).\n- The highest power of 3 is \\(3^1\\) (from 3 and 6).\n- The highest power of 7 is \\(7^1\\) (from 7).\n\nSo, the LCM is \\(2^2 \\times 3^1 \\times 7^1 = 4 \\times 3 \\times 7 = 84\\).\n\nThis means that Wanda, Darren, Beatrice, and Chi will next be together tutoring in the lab in 84 school days from today. Therefore, the answer is \\(\\boxed{84}\\).",
